     6	- Preserve local commits and uncommitted work. Fast-forward when possible; when histories diverge, preserve the local history and merge the remote branch locally. Never force-reset local work or publish unrelated local commits as part of synchronization.
     7	- Before updating a dirty checkout, protect tracked and untracked changes with recoverable backups. Restore unrelated work afterward; preserve colliding or superseded files outside the active source tree with an explicit recovery inventory rather than silently overwriting them or reintroducing obsolete implementations.
     8	- Verify that the remote merge commit is an ancestor of the primary local `main`, the delivered files exist there, and no merge conflicts remain. Report any remaining local-only commits or changes accurately; do not claim identical branches when they differ.
