    66	- 数据采集与补缺优先使用 `agent-reach` 技能：先读取其 `SKILL.md`，按目标网站选择已有后端及失败重试链。采集结果仍须进入本项目既有的解析、核验和权威存储流程，遵守来源限频，保留原始响应、来源身份、采集时间与哈希；长期数据统一保留在 NAS，不依赖已移除的 Sandisk。
    67	- Separate fetching, parsing, validation, and persistence into testable functions.
    68	- Use explicit timeouts, bounded transient retries, and existing source-specific rate limits.
    69	- Preserve raw responses for offline parsing replay; distinguish empty results from request/parser failures.
    70	- Inject credentials through environment configuration; exclude them from code, QMD, logs, and fixtures.
    71	- Parameterize SQL values; use the authoritative storage API for writes.
    72	- Use transactions; define conflicts, duplicate handling, repeated-run behavior, and rollback.
    73	- Test rollback and repeated execution; release connections/resources on both success and failure.
    74	
    75	## CI participation (owner-mandated default)
    76	
    77	- Agents do not participate in CI by default. Do not configure, add, trigger, monitor, retry, repair, or optimize CI workflows unless the user explicitly requests CI work.
    78	- Do not introduce CI coverage gaps or CI status as agent-imposed acceptance/merge gates, create CI follow-up issues, or repeatedly remind the user about CI.
    79	- Continue required local tests, reproducible QMD rendering, code review, and PI acceptance. Never report unrun or failed CI as passed.
    80	- Respect enforced GitHub branch protection. If it actually prevents an authorized merge, report that concrete blocker once; do not bypass protection or start CI remediation without explicit instruction.
    81	
    82	## Tests and acceptance
    83	
    84	### R package changes: completion gate (owner-mandated, 2026-10-17)
    85	
    86	- Any change to `packages/beidan/` (R, Python backend, Rcpp, namespace/dependencies, or tests) must be followed by a fresh normal package installation and the complete package R test suite against that installed package before the work can be considered finished. Run the complete bundled Python backend suite as well; run the repository-client phase through `Rscript tests/testthat.R` when repository-client code or that shared entry point is modified.
    87	- Targeted tests are for development only. After the final implementation/test change, rerun the complete required suites; earlier green runs and a collection of targeted reruns do not satisfy final acceptance. Existing failures, environment/path errors, and test-order conflicts must be resolved rather than dismissed as baseline debt.
    88	- Verify DLL registration and actual Rcpp wrapper calls after normal installation, using explicitly declared R libraries and the project Python interpreter. Do not use manual `dyn.load()` or mix `devtools::load_all()` with the installed package to obtain a passing result.
    89	- Any failed assertion, errored test, failed installation, or failed required check prevents completion. A skipped test is not a passed test: record its exact reason and missing evidence, and do not claim all cases verified or mark a required unavailable case complete. Never delete tests, weaken assertions, fabricate fixtures, or turn failures into skips to satisfy this gate.
    90	- Record final source identity, exact commands, exit statuses, full-suite totals, skip reasons, and corresponding regression tests in the delivery QMD. Complete clean-session rendering and `codex review` of the final artifact before reporting completion. Preserve unrelated work; do not trigger CI as part of these local checks.
    91	
    92	- Use `testthat` in `packages/beidan/tests/testthat/` for package functions and `tests/testthat/` for repository clients; use `pytest` in the relevant `tests/` area.
    93	- Map every project function to tests, including helpers and functions defined in QMD; untested existing functions remain gaps.
    94	- Add/update and run corresponding tests with each function change; bug fixes require regression tests.
    95	- Test observable behavior and contracts: normal inputs, relevant boundaries/missing/empty inputs, and failure paths.
    96	- Test third-party integration contracts; dependency internals remain the dependency's responsibility.
    97	- Exercise test helpers through the tests they support; avoid recursive tests of tests.
    98	- Keep routine tests deterministic with saved responses and temporary databases; separate live integration checks.
    99	- Run R tests with `Rscript tests/testthat.R`; run Python tests with the project interpreter's `-m pytest`.
   100	- Test Rcpp functions through their exported R wrappers, including conversion boundaries and failure paths.
   101	- Verify key QMD in a fresh process with declared inputs, execution enabled, cache/freeze bypassed, and errors fatal.
   102	- Rendering does not replace function tests; HTML containing execution errors fails acceptance.
   103	- Inspect key rendered tables/figures for missing content, units, and labels; identify input snapshots and parameters.
   104	- Verify affected function tests, data contracts, key QMD renders, and applicable cutoff governance checks locally.
   105	- Report changed behavior, function/test mapping, exact check commands/results, and reasons for skipped checks.
   106	- Every delivery must pass `codex review` covering its QMD, reusable implementation, tests, and data contracts before PI acceptance.
   107	- Record the reviewed revision or file hashes, review command, findings, and resolutions in the delivery QMD; a successful process exit alone is not acceptance.
   108	- Fix blocking findings and rerun review after relevant changes; PI verifies the final reviewed artifact before merge.
   109	- Skipped or failed required checks do not pass; documentation alone does not prove implementation or enforcement.
