   112	## Cutoff-driven historical learning (owner-mandated)
   113	
   114	### Scope and chronology
   115	
   116	- Every decision-facing historical learning, calibration, tuning, selection, ranking, gate, or optimization function must receive an explicit cutoff, either as a standalone cutoff object or embedded in an explicitly passed decision object (for example, `portfolio$cutoff`). An embedded cutoff satisfies this requirement; do not require a redundant standalone cutoff argument.
   117	- Validate the embedded cutoff and its binding to the object's input snapshots and derived artifacts. Missing, malformed, or inconsistent cutoff context must fail closed; never infer it from the current clock, hidden globals, or mutable session state. Changing the cutoff requires rebuilding the affected decision artifacts, not merely editing their cutoff field. All chronology, receipt, and cache requirements below apply equally to both forms.
   118	- This includes preprocessing, thresholds, support depth, hyperparameters, seeds, expert admission, routing, allocation, bankroll gates, league/team effects, regimes, embeddings, priors, shrinkage, imputation, normalization, and availability gates.
   119	- Admit actual source data and available labels strictly before cutoff; derive every fit/tune/calibration partition within that prior window.
   120	- Fail closed on missing chronology or insufficient history.
   121	- Use issue-level walk-forward with the target fixture-relative decision epoch as cutoff.
   122	- Admit prior-year history and current-year issues only when their labels were actually available before cutoff.
   123	- Exclude target/future issues and unsettled labels by both timestamp and exact target-issue identity, even if a bad source claims early target settlement.
   124	- Freeze an immutable cutoff-keyed artifact before opening target settlement; later labels must never rewrite it.
   125	- Name availability evidence classes: observed availability or documented conservative safe boundaries may authorize prospective use; historical timestamp proxies are diagnostic only.
   126	- Hidden globals such as `FIT_END`, `TUNE_YEAR`, `CALIBRATION_YEAR`, or detached acceptance booleans must not control new target periods.
   127	- Pre-rule historical packages may remain only as inventoried evidence, not reusable clean interfaces.
   128	- Pass business constants explicitly: fixed N, CNY1,024, CNY2 units, and one ticket-level 0.65 payout factor.
